section.para:
formal grammarrole of

The designers of Lojban built its grammar so that a formal definition can state it. A formal grammar is a precise definition that a machine can test. The designers achieved that aim to a high degree. This chapter presents two formal grammars. The first defines the word forms: which strings of letters are words in the first place, and where each word begins and ends (see
). The second defines the syntax: which strings of words are grammatical text, and what structure each such text has (see
).

Second, where a tag stands directly before a selbri, the EBNF permits more than one grouping. The BPFK is the language-definition committee, and

tells its story. The BPFK approved a decision on tag binding that picks one grouping. The parsers that this edition surveyed implement that choice (see
).

